<title>MEXICO: San Jose Accord delegates ask for pact extension.</title>
<headline>San Jose Accord delegates ask for pact extension.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delegates from the Continuing Bilateral Committee of the San Jose Accord said in a statement that they will ask both Mexico and Venezuela to renew the accord for a period from August 1997 to July 1998.</p>
<p>The accord was first signed in 1980 to help provide oil supplies to 11 countries in Central America and the Caribbean.</p>
<p>The statement, released by the Mexican Energy Ministry, said daily sales between August 1996 and May 1997 under the pact were 128,000 barrels of petroleum and derivatives.</p>
<p>The statement was released on Sunday.</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
